 ### [Frequency Regularization](6130-frequency-regularization.md)
-Frequency regularization constrains the spectral content of the rendered output to guide Gaussian densification toward high-frequency regions. It solves the problem where standard 3D Gaussian Splatting initialization and densification may fail to capture fine geometric details or high-frequency textures, leading to blurry reconstructions. Unlike [Smoothed 2D Supervision](7213-smoothed-2d-supervision.md) which operates in the spatial domain via kernel smoothing, or [Depth Regularization](7616-depth-regularization.md) which enforces geometric consistency, frequency regularization operates in the spectral domain to explicitly encourage the representation of high-frequency signal components.
