 ### [3D Half-Gaussian Splatting Covariance Transformation and Regularization](9150-3d-half-gaussian-splatting-covariance-transformation-and-reg.md)
-3D Half-Gaussian Splatting (3D-HGS) modifies the standard 3D Gaussian kernel into a half-ellipsoid to better model sharp surface boundaries and occlusions, addressing the "blooming" artifacts common in full Gaussians near object edges. It achieves this by transforming the covariance matrix into a local basis aligned with a splitting plane normal, projecting the covariance to enforce zero variance along the normal direction, and then transforming it back to world space. This method builds on [Regularization and Geometry Constraints](6269-regularization-and-geometry-constraints.md) by applying a structural constraint to the Gaussian parameters themselves rather than an auxiliary loss term.
