 ### [Cross-scale geometric adaptation](10796-cross-scale-geometric-adaptation.md)
-Cross-scale geometric adaptation is a self-adaptive regularization technique that uses reprojection errors across multiple voxel scales to guide geometry learning without requiring explicit depth ground truth. It selects render depths with minimal reprojection error across different scales as pseudo labels, ensuring geometric integrity and reducing floaters more effectively than single-scale depth priors. Unlike siblings that rely on fixed schedules or external priors, this method dynamically adapts to scene frequencies by leveraging low-resolution voxels for coarse geometry early in training and high-resolution voxels for detail refinement later.
